Build against the LikeOS C library headers.

hdparm takes its kernel interface from a handful of system headers (the
__u8 .. __u64 types, the BLK* and HDIO_* requests, byte order helpers,
the optical drive packet interface).  On LikeOS these are in the C library:
<sys/mount.h> (BLK*), <sys/hdreg.h> (HDIO_*), <scsi/sg.h> (SG_IO), and the
rest is gathered in the port's likeos-hdparm.h.  Each include is switched
under __LIKEOS__, the upstream line stays as it is in the other branch.

MAP_LOCKED for the firmware image of --fwdownload is 0 on LikeOS, the way
hdparm already handles a system without MAP_POPULATE: memory is never paged
out there, so the populated mapping stays resident anyway.

